                <pb facs="0501" n="321" sameAs="frus:frus1945Berlinv02/pg321"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00119 EAC/7–2345: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Ambassador in the United Kingdom</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Winant</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Babelsberg</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1945-07-23">July 23, 1945</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Victory</hi> 241.
                    To AmEmbassy London for Winant. Info
                    [Acting] SecState Washington.</p>
                <p>(Message has been sent to MA, London.)</p>
                <p>Gousev informed Mosely tonight instructions sent Saksin last night or this morning to sign EAC agreement on additional requirements.<anchor
                        n="1" xml:id="d710a-84-f1"/></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Byrnes</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
